<title>HUNGARY: HUNGARIAN, POLISH SHARES PULL CESI INDEX LOWER.</title>
<headline>HUNGARIAN, POLISH SHARES PULL CESI INDEX LOWER.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The CESI Central European Share Index fell on Monday to close at 1,463.14 points, down 10.51 points or 0.71 percent, the Budapest Stock Stock Exchange said on its Reuters page.</p>
<p>The index was pulled down by losing Hungarian and Czech shares.</p>
<p>The index, which has been published since February 1, reflects trends of 50 shares on the Budapest, Prague and Warsaw bourses.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327-4040</p>
</text>
